        role: "Pediatrician",
        exam: [.direct("What did you see when {V} was brought to you on {DATE}?", "\"A five-month-old with a swollen leg. The parents said {V} had been fine at drop-off and swollen at pickup.\""), .direct("What did the scan show?", "\"A fracture of the leg bone. It was a clean break that fit a significant force.\""), .direct("Is a fracture like that consistent with a fall from a mat?", "\"No. A short slip from a mat would not usually produce that kind of fracture in an infant.\""), .direct("What do the parents report?", "\"That {V} was fine at drop-off. They noticed the swelling later at pickup. {D} had texted that {V} was fussy.\""), .direct("What did your examination add?", "\"Tenderness and swelling localized to the leg, and a baby who cried when it was moved.\""), .direct("Who was with {V} that day?", "\"{DL}, a day care worker, was alone with {V} at the relevant time, according to the history.\""), .direct("What did the parents tell you about the child's condition that morning?", "\"They said the baby was fine at drop-off at eight, eating and moving normally. By pickup at five the leg was swollen, and the baby cried when it was touched.\""), .cross("Could a fall have caused this fracture?", "\"Rarely. I would not exclude it entirely, but it would be unusual from a mat.\""), .cross("Did you find other injuries?", "\"No. I did not see bruising elsewhere or signs of other trauma.\""), .cross("Did {DL} tell you what happened?", "\"I was told {DL} said {V} slipped from a mat. I do not have a first-hand account.\""), .cross("How long was {V} at day care that day?", "\"I understand several hours. I cannot give you a precise number.\""), .cross("Could a medical condition weaken infant bones?", "\"It can, but I did not find a sign of that. I would test if it were suspected.\"")],
        defenseRole: "Second pediatrician",
        defenseExam: [.direct("What is your field?", "\"I am a pediatrician with experience reviewing infant injuries.\""), .direct("Can a fall from a mat fracture an infant leg?", "\"Rarely, but it can happen. A hard landing with a twist can do it.\""), .direct("Have you seen such cases?", "\"Occasionally. It is not common, but it is documented in the literature.\""), .direct("What factors matter?", "\"How the leg twisted, the surface, and the infant's bone density. A thin mat adds little cushion.\""), .direct("Did you review the imaging here?", "\"Yes. The fracture pattern is compatible with a twisting injury, which can happen in a slip.\""), .direct("Is the history provided consistent?", "\"It can be. A slip with a twist and an immediate cry fits.\""), .direct("What would you need to see to decide a fracture came from a fall from a mat?", "\"I would look at the type of fracture, the height of the fall, and the surface. A mat only a half inch thick gives little cushioning on a hard floor underneath.\""), .direct("Can you say from the scan alone that someone intentionally hurt the infant?", "\"No. A scan shows the break, not how it happened. Accidents, including short falls, can cause the same pattern, though they are less common than other causes.\""), .cross("Is that the most likely cause?", "\"I would not say most likely. Other causes are possible.\""), .cross("Did you examine {V}?", "\"No. I reviewed the records and images only.\""), .cross("Could an inflicted injury look the same?", "\"It could. That is why the history matters so much.\""), .cross("Would a delay in telling parents concern you?", "\"Yes. Prompt reporting is important for any infant injury.\""), .cross("Did you speak to {DL}?", "\"No. I only reviewed the records.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} hurt an infant.", "A mat fall."),
        allocution: "\"I wasn't the person I wanted to be that day. I care for infants, and I feed them, change them, and play with them every day. {V} slipped off the edge of the play mat, and I heard a cry and picked {V.him} up. I'm sorry that {V.he} was hurt on my watch.\"",
