        openings: ("After a windstorm, {D}, a fence contractor, took $112,000 in advances from nineteen homeowners and finished only two fences. No license was on record, and {D.he} changed phone numbers.", "The defense will present evidence that lumber was scarce, that {D} meant to build the fences, and that {D.he} finished two before things fell apart."),
        closings: ("Nineteen homeowners, $112,000 in advances, no license, a changed phone number, and only two fences finished. {D} took money from storm victims and then went silent.", "A contractor overwhelmed after a windstorm, with lumber that was scarce for weeks. The State must prove {D} never meant to do the work, and it has not."),
