        allocution: "\"I let money decide it, and I can't take it back, if I did. Those reimbursement checks were for travel I took for the union, and I believed the board had approved them, according to the minutes. I lost many of my receipts over the years. I'm sorry to the members.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} had no receipts for $80,000.", "Board minutes mention travel in general."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you write checks to yourself for trips you took?", "\"Yes. For travel I took for the union. I believed the board had approved it, based on the minutes.\""), .direct("Where are the receipts for the travel you were reimbursed for?", "\"I lost many of them over the years. I kept some, but not all, and I know that is a problem.\""), .direct("Did the board approve travel for you in those meetings?", "\"In general terms, in the minutes. I treated that as approval, and I did not ask for more detail.\""), .direct("Please tell us about your time as treasurer.", "\"I served as treasurer for several years. I handled dues, paid bills, and traveled for the union to conferences and negotiations.\""), .direct("What were the reimbursement checks for?", "\"They were for travel I took for the union. I paid costs myself and wrote reimbursement checks, which is how I understood the process.\""), .direct("What do you say about the board's approval?", "\"The board approved travel in general. I took that to cover my trips, and I did not ask for a vote each time.\""), .cross("No trips are booked in the travel records, are they?", "\"I booked some myself, outside the system. The records may be incomplete, and I should have kept better ones.\""), .cross("You have no receipts for $80,000 of those checks, do you?", "\"No. I know that. I did not keep them, and I cannot tell you every trip that they covered.\""), .cross("$110,000 over three years. How many trips did that cover?", "\"I do not have an exact count. It was a lot of travel, and I cannot list every one.\""), .cross("You signed the reimbursement checks yourself without anyone countersigning, didn't you?", "\"I signed them myself, yes. No one else had to countersign, because that was how the union had always done it.\""), .cross("You have no receipts for most of the money, do you?", "\"Not for most of it. I kept some, and the rest was lost in a move. I know that is not good enough.\"")],
        openings: ("A local's treasurer, {D}, wrote reimbursement checks to {D.himself} for trips that no record shows were booked, totaling $110,000 over three years. A member says no one approved them, and $80,000 has no receipts.", "Weigh the defense proof, which will show that board minutes mention travel in general terms and that {D} believed the reimbursements were approved as union business."),
        closings: ("$110,000 in checks to the treasurer for trips no record shows, no approval from members, and no receipts for $80,000. The dues belonged to the members.", "Board minutes that mention travel and a treasurer who lost receipts. The State must prove {D} did not travel and meant to steal."),
